  "title": "netlink: fix selected bytes for padding",
  "description": "At that point of the code, offset points to the beginning of the payload\nof the attribute. The padding starts at the signaled length of the\nattribute (which includes the header), so the padding starts at\noffset + signaled length - header size (4).\n\nAlso attaching the padding to the attribute tree instead of the global\ntree makes more sense.\n\n### Before patch\n![Pasted_image](/uploads/9fb2e007cb781530002610094c2ec9da/Pasted_image.png)\n\n### After patch\n![Pasted_image__2_](/uploads/0615cfa6d9294f68dc6a7c4ef85bb02b/Pasted_image__2_.png)\n\n### PCAP sample to test the fix\n[netlink.pcap](/uploads/8b47e9fa482424111951e83a35b9ef22/netlink.pcap)",
